   "format": "short_answer",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let r(x) = (x + 4) / ((x + 1)(x^2 - 6x + 8)). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which r is continuous. What is the sum of the integers in that interval?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The quadratic factors as x^2 - 6x + 8 = (x - 2)(x - 4), so the denominator is zero at x = -1, x = 2 and x = 4, and those three inputs are excluded.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               1
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               4
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "r is a rational function, and a rational function is continuous at every input of its domain, so r is continuous on (-infinity, -1) U (-1, 2) U (2, 4) U (4, infinity).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               4
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Add",
                  "x",
                  1
               ],
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  4
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece that contains x = 0 is (-1, 2), open at both ends. Its integers are 0 and 1.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            0,
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The sum of those integers is 1.",
         "mathjson": 1
      }
   ],
